Senior Mechanical/HVAC Engineer

We are seeking a Senior Mechanical/HVAC Engineer to join our team and lead the design and delivery of Heating, Ventilation, and Air Conditioning systems, along with related building services. The role focuses on reliable, efficient, and compliant mechanical systems for a variety of facilities, including data center environments, with emphasis on collaboration and clear communication across project teams.

About the Role:
- Lead mechanical system design, analysis, and documentation for HVAC and building services projects
- Coordinate with clients, architects, and other engineering disciplines to deliver integrated solutions
- Ensure compliance with applicable codes, standards, and project requirements
- Guide risk assessment, quality assurance, and project execution activities
- Support commissioning, handover, and lifecycle considerations for installed systems

Required Skills:
- Heating, Ventilation, and Air Conditioning (HVAC) design and optimization
- Mechanical engineering fundamentals
- Building services engineering
- Data Center facilities and critical environment considerations
- Risk assessment and mitigation
- Design and engineering design methodologies

Responsibilities:
- Develop concepts, calculations, and detailed design deliverables for mechanical systems
- Prepare and review drawings, specifications, and documents
- Perform technical reviews and coordinate with internal teams and external stakeholders
- Monitor project scope, schedule, and budget implications related to mechanical systems
- Support energy efficiency initiatives and reliability improvements

Preferred Qualifications:
- Bachelor's or Master's degree in Mechanical Engineering or a related field
- Professional licensure (e.g., PE) or equivalent
- Experience with data center environments is advantageous
- Strong communication, teamwork, and problem-solving skills

What We Offer:
- A collaborative and inclusive work environment
- Opportunities for professional growth, new challenges, and exposure to diverse projects
- Flexible work arrangements and professional development support

To Apply:
- Please submit your resume and a short cover letter outlining your relevant experience and interest in this role.

We look forward to reviewing your application for the Senior Mechanical/HVAC Engineer position.